2026-09-27T10:21:15.0701682Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0701882Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0702180Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0702450Z 
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0702541Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0702750Z ================
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0703951Z 
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0704143Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0704505Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0704713Z 
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0704825Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0705088Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0705254Z 
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0705386Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0705772Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0706110Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0706740Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0707255Z 
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0707362Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0708130Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0708663Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0708932Z 
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0709217Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0709604Z 
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0709686Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0709869Z ========
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0709978Z 
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0711221Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0712527Z 
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0712739Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0713188Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0714040Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0714635Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0715179Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0787904Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0788711Z 
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0788825Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0789085Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0789233Z 
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0790279Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0791436Z 
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0792070Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0792930Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:21:15.0793152Z 
